<article class="env-lemma" id="00FQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00FQ">Lemma <span data-tag="00FQ">10.31.5</span>.</a> If $R$ is a Noetherian ring then $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is a Noetherian topological space, see Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/0051" data-tag="0051">5.9.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is because any closed subset of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is uniquely of the form $V(I)$ with $I$ a radical ideal, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00E0" data-tag="00E0">10.17.2</a>. And this correspondence is inclusion reversing. Thus the result follows from the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>